{"id":"n-20261029-iyuwia","category":"gaming","display_title":"UK Budget Tax Hike Threatens Racing","display_title_he":"העלת מס בתקציב בריטניה מאיימת על מרוצי הסוסים","short_summary":"A recent increase in gaming machine duty in the UK budget has sparked concerns among racing officials over potential betting shop closures and significant financial losses for the sport.","english_level":"C1","words":435,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"The Guardian","domain":"theguardian.com","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/28/horse-racing-chief-warning-budget-fixed-odds-gaming-tax","title":"British racing chief warns budget tax hike may have ‘devastating’ impact on sport","published_at":"2026-10-28T17:35:50.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-28T17:35:50.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-29T07:14:16.375Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The governing body for British horse racing has expressed deep concern following a recent government decision to increase taxation on gaming machines located in high street betting shops. According to statements released on Wednesday, the newly delivered budget by Chancellor John Healey included an upward adjustment in the duty levied on profits generated from fixed-odds gaming machines, moving the applicable rate from twenty percent to twenty-five percent.","While the Social Market Foundation thinktank had previously advocated for a much steeper increase to forty percent to address the higher harms associated with this specific form of gambling, the officially implemented rise was ultimately more moderate. Nevertheless, Brant Dunshea, the chief executive of the British Horseracing Authority, cautioned that even this measured five percent adjustment could prove devastating for the sport. He noted a clear and present risk that hundreds, if not thousands, of betting establishments across the nation might face closure as a direct consequence of the policy.","The broader financial implications for British racing could be exceptionally severe because the industry relies heavily on physical betting shops for a substantial portion of its overall funding. Independent modelling that was shared with the Treasury prior to the budget presentation indicates that the sport could potentially lose up to fifty-seven million pounds annually. British racing currently derives nearly a third of its total three-hundred-and-fifty-million-pound yearly income through the financial levy and rights payments for live coverage and data associated with high street bookmakers. Industry leaders warned that such dramatic revenue losses would directly impact prize money, the long-term viability of racecourses, thousands of jobs, and vital horse welfare projects and research initiatives.","Furthermore, the potential wave of closures threatens a cornerstone of the sport's community engagement. For a large part of the sport's dedicated fanbase, visiting a local bookie remains the primary way to interact with horse racing. Despite the grave warnings voiced by racing executives, the immediate market response to the budget announcement diverged significantly. Share prices for major high-street gambling corporations, including Entain—the owner of Ladbrokes and Coral—and Evoke, which owns William Hill, experienced noticeable increases shortly after the chancellor delivered his speech.","As the situation continues to develop, the British Horseracing Authority plans to urgently engage with government officials to establish collaborative ways to reduce the impact and navigate the fallout. Meanwhile, observers note that Gideon Salutin, co-founder of the report by the Social Market Foundation, expressed satisfaction that the duty was raised to reflect gambling harms, yet remained sceptical that such a relatively limited five percent rise would have a significant impact on corporate industry behavior or prevent high-street venue closures."],"facts":[{"fact":"Chancellor John Healey raised the duty on fixed-odds gaming machine profits from 20% to 25% in his first budget.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Brant Dunshea, chief executive of the British Horseracing Authority, warned the tax hike could have a devastating impact, risking hundreds or thousands of betting shop closures.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"British racing generates nearly a third of its £350 million annual income from high street betting shops, and independent modelling suggests potential losses of up to £57 million a year.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The Social Market Foundation thinktank had recommended doubling the machine games duty from 20% to 40%.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Shares in major gambling companies such as Entain and Evoke rose following the budget announcement.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"governing","lemma":"govern","pos":"verb","he":"ממשלה / מנהל","name":false},{"text":"body","lemma":"body","pos":"noun","he":"גוף","name":false},{"text":"British","lemma":"British","pos":"adjective","he":"בריטי","name":"British"},{"text":"horse","lemma":"horse","pos":"noun","he":"סוס","name":false},{"text":"racing","lemma":"racing","pos":"noun","he":"מרוצים","name":false},{"text":"expressed","lemma":"express","pos":"verb","he":"הביע","name":false},{"text":"deep","lemma":"deep","pos":"adjective","he":"עמוק","name":false},{"text":"concern","lemma":"concern","pos":"noun","he":"דאגה","name":false},{"text":"recent","lemma":"recent","pos":"adjective","he":"נוכחי / אחרון","name":false},{"text":"government","lemma":"government","pos":"noun","he":"ממשלה","name":false},{"text":"decision","lemma":"decision","pos":"noun","he":"החלטה","name":false},{"text":"increase","lemma":"increase","pos":"verb","he":"להגדיל","name":false},{"text":"taxation","lemma":"taxation","pos":"noun","he":"מיסוי","name":false},{"text":"gaming","lemma":"gaming","pos":"noun","he":"משחקי הימור","name":false},{"text":"machines","lemma":"machine","pos":"noun","he":"מכונות","name":false}